A renaming moves a chunk, or every chunk of a module, to another path. With items set it moves an item, or every item of a domain.
@<rewrite@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type renaming struct {
	module bool
	items  bool
	// The module path or domain; a chunk or an item has its own name last.
	from, to []Name
}

@~ Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.Name @? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.renaming @
A fileMove sends a file, or every file below a directory, to another path.
@<rewrite@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type fileMove struct {
	from, to string
	dir      bool
}

@? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.fileMove @
fileMoves is a batch of file or directory moves applied together during mv or rm.
@<rewrite@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type fileMoves []fileMove

@~ Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.fileMove @? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.fileMoves @
A fileIndex tells where each file visible in a node comes from.
@<rewrite@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type fileIndex struct {
	own map[string]bool // files of the node's own blocks
	// Files of the base nodes and mapped paths, with their source.
	// A mapped directory keeps its trailing slash.
	other map[string]string
}

@? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.fileIndex @
Input schema for the rename MCP tool, specifying the composition, node, target chunk, module, item, or domain ref, and new path.
@<mcp@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type renameIn struct {
	Composition string `json:"composition" jsonschema:"ref of the composition"`
	Node        string `json:"node" jsonschema:"ref of the node"`
	Object      string `json:"object" jsonschema:"ref of a chunk or module of the chunk tree, or of an item or domain of the item tree"`
	To          string `json:"to" jsonschema:"new path, such as Module@@/chunk"`
}

@~ Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.Node @? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.renameIn @
Input schema for the operate_files MCP tool, specifying the composition, node, and rm or mv file command.
@<mcp@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type filesIn struct {
	Composition string `json:"composition" jsonschema:"ref of the composition"`
	Node        string `json:"node" jsonschema:"ref of the node"`
	Command     string `json:"command" jsonschema:"one rm or mv command, such as mv src/a.c lib/"`
}

@~ Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.Node @? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.filesIn @
Tests of rewrite.go.
@[internal/litar/rewrite_test.go@`go module@`go tests@=
@<rewrite test@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/file@>@
@<rewrite test@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/import paths@+
"os"
"path/filepath"
"strings"
"testing"
@
renameRoot is the root archive fixture used by chunk and module rename tests.
@<rewrite test@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/constants@+
const renameRoot = `About one.
@@<Mod@@/one@@=
1 @@<.@@/Sub@@/two@@> @@<x@@:Mod@@/three@@|Mod@@/Sub@@/filter@@>
@@| Mod@@/Sub@@/filter @@
@@<Mod@@/Sub@@/two@@=
2 @@<..@@/three@@> @@<other@@>
@@
@@<Mod@@/Sub@@/filter@@=
#!/bin/sh
cat
@@
@@<Chunk@@/Mod@@/Sub@@={"description": "sub"}@@
@@<Chunk@@/Mod@@/one@@={"description": "one"}@@
@@<other@@=o@@
@@<Mod@@/three@@=3@@
`

@? Project@/litar@/Go@/constants@/litar.renameRoot @
renameChild is the child archive fixture used by chunk and module rename tests.
@<rewrite test@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/constants@+
const renameChild = `@@<lab@@:Mod@@/one@@+
more @@<Mod@@/Sub@@/two@@>
@@
`

@? Project@/litar@/Go@/constants@/litar.renameChild @
filesRoot is the root archive fixture used by file move and removal tests.
@<rewrite test@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/variables@+
var filesRoot = strings.ReplaceAll(`@@[src/a.c@@'sources@@=
a
@@
@@(src/sub/b.sh@@=
b
@@
@@<src/a.c@@+
more
@@
@@<File@@/src@@={"description": "sources"}@@
@@<File@@/src@@/a.c@@={"description": "a"}@@
@@<list@@=
@@<src/a.c@@> @@<@@|cat@@,src/a.c@@!src/sub/b.sh@@+sources@@>
@@
@@<cat@@=
#!/bin/sh
cat
@@
@@[keep.txt@@=k@@
`, "'", "\x60")

@? Project@/litar@/Go@/variables@/litar.filesRoot @
filesChild is the child archive fixture used by file move and removal tests.
@<rewrite test@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/constants@+
const filesChild = `@@<use@@=
@@<src/a.c@@>
@@
@@[own.txt@@=o@@
`

