@
A unit is a functional unit that a node selects: a chunk reference, an item, or a file.
Exactly one of its fields is set.
@<list@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type unit struct {
	chunk *ChunkRef
	item  Item
	file  string
}

@~ Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.ChunkRef @~ Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.Item @? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.unit @
@<compose@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/import paths@+
"slices"
@
readOnlyNode serves a mapped directory of the ground: reads go through to the host,
and every operation that would change the host fails with EROFS.
@<fuse@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/types@+
type readOnlyNode struct {
	*fs.LoopbackNode
}

@? Project@/litar@/Go@/types@/litar.readOnlyNode @
The archive of TestSelection has a block for each rule. Selecting 'body': 'step' and 'fmt'
are construction blocks, through Ca and Cf edges; 'call def' defines an item that 'body'
refers to, but 'call inner', its construction block, is not followed; 'main.c' and
'container' contain selected chunks; 'user of x' refers to an item that a construction block
defines, but 'user of call' to one that only 'call def' defines; 'other' invokes the
selected filter, and Cf edges are not stepped back.
@<eval test@:litar@:Language@/Go@/File@/variables@+
var selectionArchive = "" +
	"@@[main.c@@=\n@@<body@@>\n@@\n" +
	"@@<body@@=\n@@<step@@>\n@@|fmt@@~ K@@/call @@\n" +
	"@@<step@@=\nx++;\n@@? K@@/x @@\n" +
	"@@<fmt@@=cat@@\n" +
	"@@<other@@=\ny\n@@|fmt@@\n" +
	"@@<call def@@=\n@@<call inner@@>\n@@? K@@/call @@\n" +
	"@@<call inner@@=inner();@@\n" +
	"@@<user of x@@=use(x);\n@@~ K@@/x @@\n" +
	"@@<user of call@@=call();\n@@~ K@@/call @@\n" +
	"@@<container@@=\n@@<call def@@>\n@@\n"

@? Project@/litar@/Go@/variables@/litar.selectionArchive @
