@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/add each file of 'cat' to 'root', its directories as branches@=
{"description": "Inserts each catalog entry into the file tree by splitting its slash-separated path into branch nodes, adding non-directory and archive files as leaves and walking mapped host directories."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/add each item of 'blocks' to 'root', its domains as branches@=
{"description": "Inserts every item referenced by the blocks into the item tree, creating branch nodes for each domain segment and a leaf for the final name."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/add the file chunk of 'b' to 'root' below File@=
{"description": "Places a file block's chunk under the reserved File subtree by splitting its path on slashes into directory branches and a final file leaf."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/add the files below the origin of 'f' to the branch 'last' of 'cur'@=
{"description": "Walks a mapped directory's host origin with filepath.WalkDir to populate subdirectories and file leaves under its tree branch, leaving missing or unreadable directories as empty branches."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/add the label path of 'labels' under 'root', the last label first@=
{"description": "Walks a label slice in reverse order (least specific first) to create and index nested specNode entries under the specialization tree root."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/add the modules and chunks of 'blocks' outside the reserved namespaces to 'root'@=
{"description": "Populates the chunk tree from non-reserved blocks, routing root-module file chunks under the File branch and adding module paths as branches with chunk names as leaves."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/add the resources and resource templates of 'a'@=
{"description": "Registers all fixed MCP resources and URI resource templates on the server, routing every read through a single URI-dispatching handler."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/append to 't' the leaf of the entry 'e'@=
{"description": "Constructs a leaf treeJSON node with its optional leaf description and appends it to the parent tree's subtrees."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/append to 't' the subtree of the module entry 'e'@=
{"description": "Copies the current module path, extends it with the submodule name, and recursively appends the submodule's treeJSON subtree with its description."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/build the tree of the node 'n' and the nodes on it@=
{"description": "Recursively converts a composition node and its child nodes into a treeJSON structure, marking every node as an addressable leaf."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/build the tree of the specialization 'n', described from 'meta'@=
{"description": "Recursively builds a specialization treeJSON node, reversing its path and joining with @@: to look up its description in meta."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/cases of 'kind' in 'selectBlocks' that take one ref@=
{"description": "Switch cases in selectBlocks handling single-reference queries: refer (blocks carrying an item), specialization (blocks matching an exact label path), and define (blocks defining an item)."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/collect in 'files' the paths of the file blocks of 'blocks'@=
{"description": "Scans the block slice and records the path of every file block in the files lookup map."}
@
@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/ensure the labels of every reference to 'chunk' in 'blocks'@=
{"description": "Walks block headers, resolved inner chunk references, and resolved filter references to register every label path targeting the selected chunk (or all chunks)."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/fail unless the catalog file 'f' at 'path' is defined exactly once@=
{"description": "Returns an error if the catalog entry for path is missing or defined as both an archive file and a host mapping."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/find the 'root' of 'w' and group the other nodes by base in 'children'@=
{"description": "Scans the composition's nodes to identify the root node (empty base) and index all other nodes by their formatted base path."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/read 'f' into 'data', from its origin or by evaluating 'path'@=
{"description": "Reads a mapped file directly from its host origin, or unlocks the server mutex while evaluating an archive file chunk with evalReporting."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/record 'desc' in 'meta' for the 'target' of the namespace 'ns'@=
{"description": "Stores a parsed meta description in the Chunk, Specialization, File, or Index map of metaInfo according to its reserved namespace."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/record the place of 'node' at 'path' in 'out', then walk its subtrees@=
{"description": "Records a copied path and leaf flag for a tree node by its ref in the index map, then recursively walks each subtree."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/set 'desc' to the description in the meta chunk 'ref'@=
{"description": "Evaluates a meta chunk reference on the chain and parses its JSON description field, wrapping parse errors with the chunk reference."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/MCP Server@/tools of the MCP server of 'a'@=
{"description": "Registers all 15 MCP tools on the server with their descriptions, handlers, and explicit nullable or array input schemas where needed."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Parser@/add 'name' to 'labels' or to 'module', as the control 'kind' after it says@=
{"description": "Validates a header name segment against ordering, emptiness, and relative-name rules, appending it to labels or module and handling an explicit leading root slash."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Parser@/cases of the control 'kind' in the body 'b', after the content 'text'@=
{"description": "Switch cases in body parsing for inner chunk references (@@<), filter pipelines (@@|), and item definitions or references (@@?, @@~)."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Parser@/cases of the control 'kind' that opens the block 'b' in 'p'@=
{"description": "Dispatches block opening controls to parse a chunk block (@@<), a regular file block (@@[), or an executable file block (@@()."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Parser@/check that the control 'kind' after the sets is the operation of a file@=
{"description": "Verifies that a file header ends with the set operation (@@=), rejecting extension (@@+), EOF, or any other control."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Parser@/read into 'sets' the sets of the file, moving 'kind' past them@=
{"description": "Loops over backquote controls (@@`) in a file header, reading and validating non-empty file set names."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Parser@/read into 'view' the view operations of 'ref', moving 'kind' past them@=
{"description": "Loops over view operation controls (+, -, ,, !) after a filter reference, reading each non-empty operand name into the view list."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Rewrite@/collect in 'moved' the chunks 'r' renames below 'n' and in 'taken' the others, failing if 'n' renames none@=
{"description": "Walks the node subtree to partition blocks into renamed targets and unchanged chunk keys, rejecting file blocks and failing if the target node renames nothing."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Rewrite@/fail if a chunk of 'moved' is already in 'taken'@=
{"description": "Checks every renamed chunk target against the set of existing unchanged chunk keys and returns a collision error on conflict."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Rewrite@/fail unless 'arch' has blocks, all applied to the reference of block 'i' of 'n'@=
{"description": "Validates replacement archive text for an override, requiring at least one block and matching chunk reference and file flag against the overridden block."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Rewrite@/rewrite the own blocks of 'n' with 'edit', compact them, and append the result to 'all'@=
{"description": "Applies a raw-text rewrite function to each own block of a node, re-parses and compacts the archive, and queues the pending write."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Rewrite@/save 'kept' as the mappings of 'n', restoring them if the composer cannot be written@=
{"description": "Persists updated node mappings to composer.json when any were removed, rolling back the in-memory slice if saving fails."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Rewrite@/start the comment of 'arch' where the comment of block 'i' started@=
{"description": "Transfers the leading whitespace of the overridden block's comment onto the replacement block's comment to preserve archive spacing."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Rewrite@/unmap 'arg' from 'kept', or note the files it names in 'gone' and 'lines'@=
{"description": "Removes a matching host mapping for an rm argument, or resolves archive file paths to delete while enforcing -f and -r directory rules."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Selection@=
{"description": "Steps of the functions that select the blocks reachable from a node's functional units."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Selection@/walk from the blocks applied to the unit 'u', or defining it@=
{"description": "Starts the selection reachability walk from a chunk reference, a file path chunk, or every block in the chain that defines a selected item."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Selection@/walk the references and filters of the block 'i' under 'applied'@=
{"description": "Resolves and walks each inner chunk reference and its filters, as well as the block's own filters, under the applied label path."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Command Line@/check the archives FindArchive finds in 'dir' and 'sub'@=
{"description": "Verifies that FindArchive resolves nested and nearest composer nodes and returns errors for undeclared stray or missing archives."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Command Line@/checks of running litar on 'a.la'@=
{"description": "Tests CLI invocations for printing, literal output, missing chunks, empty depend queries, and missing archive files."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Command Line@/write a composition in 'dir' with a child archive under 'sub', and another composition in 'sub'@=
{"description": "Sets up nested test directories with a parent composer declaring a child archive under a subdirectory that has its own separate composer."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/archive texts and the order orderOwn gives their blocks@=
{"description": "Table of test cases for orderOwn covering included-after-includer ordering, labels, relative modules, multi-block chunks, cycles, self-inclusion, and comment attachment."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/change to an empty directory in 'dir'@=
{"description": "Creates an empty subdirectory and switches the test working directory into it so ground resolution must use LITAR_LIBRARY."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/check a composition created in 'dir' without a ground@=
{"description": "Verifies that CreateComposedArchive with an empty ground writes an empty composer.json with a nil Ground and no nodes."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/check that 'comp' keeps the archive of the bare node as written@=
{"description": "Reloads the composer and verifies that the bare node's relative ArchiveSpec is preserved verbatim as 'bare.la'."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/check that 'w' refuses to edit its ground node@=
{"description": "Asserts that DeleteNode, ApplyBlock, DeleteChunk, and DeleteFile all fail with a ground-definition error on a ground node."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/check that 'w' tells root from root/root@=
{"description": "Verifies that node lookup distinguishes the root node from a child node also named root under it."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/check that ApplyBlock writes top before the chunks it includes in 'arch'@=
{"description": "Applies a top block referencing sub and c and checks that the written archive places top before both included chunks."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/check that CreateNode creates the empty archive 'fresh'@=
{"description": "Checks that CreateNode creates a zero-byte regular archive file, persists the node in composer.json, and accepts subsequent ApplyBlock calls."}
@

@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Tests@/Composer@/check that CreateNode does not create a missing directory@=
{"description": "Verifies that CreateNode fails when the archive's parent directory does not exist and leaves no directory behind."}
