@<Chunk@/Project@/litar@/Evaluator@/add the expansion of each block matching 'ref' to 'acc'@=
{"description": "Iterates e.byChunk[chunkKey(ref)], expanding matching blocks and replacing acc on set or joining with a newline/concatenating on extend."}
@
A set block replaces what came before. An extension whose content ended with a line break
is joined with a line feed, unless nothing came before; otherwise it is concatenated.
@<Project@/litar@/Evaluator@/add the expansion of each block matching 'ref' to 'acc'@=
for _, b := range e.byChunk[chunkKey(ref)] {
	if !matchRef(b.Ref, ref) {
		continue
	}
	matched = true
	text, err := e.expandBlock(b, ref)
	if err != nil {
		return "", err
	}
	switch {
	case b.Op == OpSet:
		acc = text
	case b.EndsLine && acc != "":
		acc += "\n" + text
	default:
		acc += text
	}
}
